(function(){"use strict";window.EDMUND_DSE_LISTENING_2018_TRANSCRIPT=Object.freeze({"partA":{"1":[{"start":0.02,"end":8.37,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task 1. Katie Chandra is the editor of the magazine. She is holding a meeting with two"},{"start":8.37,"end":17.38,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"journalists, Iris Mu and Dan Lai, about the next issue. Listen to their discussion and"},{"start":17.38,"end":24.49,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"complete the missing information in the spaces below. One has been provided as an example."},{"start":26.19,"end":33.94,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have thirty seconds to study the task. At the end of the task, you will have one"},{"start":33.94,"end":71.63,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"minute to tidy up your answers. Morning, Dan. You look very well. Where's Katie?"},{"start":72.29,"end":79.03,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Hi, Iris. She's not here yet, but she texted to say she's on her way. So, um, how was"},{"start":79.03,"end":82.23,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"your weekend? Oh, really terrible, actually."},{"start":82.97,"end":87.83,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Oh, dear. I'm sorry to hear that. What was so awful about it?"},{"start":88.39,"end":94.19,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Well, my dog was sick. Oh, no. Um, why was your dog sick?"},{"start":94.91,"end":101.29,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"I don't know. It was fine all week. And then suddenly, at the weekend, it became really,"},{"start":101.29,"end":107.07,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"really sick. Oh, that's terrible. Well, I hope your dog gets better soon."},{"start":107.37,"end":114.69,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Thanks. How about you? How was yours? Well, I don't mean to gloat, but I had a great weekend."},{"start":114.69,"end":122.68,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"A really wonderful weekend. Do you want to know why? Let me tell you. I bought a new TV,"},{"start":123.22,"end":129.74,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"one of those really, really big TVs. It's totally amazing. It's like real life."},{"start":129.96,"end":137.14,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Wow. That sounds cool. I would love to have a big TV like that. Oh, here comes Katie"},{"start":137.14,"end":141.78,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"now. Morning, guys. Sorry, I'm a bit late. Morning, Katie."},{"start":142.56,"end":148.24,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"So, how was your weekend, Katie? Boring, boring, boring."},{"start":148.64,"end":157.04,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Why, why, why? Because I had to work, work, work, Dan. That's my reward for being the"},{"start":157.04,"end":161.9,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"boss, I suppose, having to work all weekend. Oh, well."},{"start":162.68,"end":168.54,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Right now, we've got lots to get through. So, for the June edition of the magazine,"},{"start":169.14,"end":176.66,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"our main theme will be games and play. Now, I sent out an email last week asking us all to"},{"start":176.66,"end":183.6,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"come up with ideas for topics. Dan? Well, I was thinking of computer games and learning,"},{"start":184.16,"end":191.2,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"you know, like games that actually teach you a skill. There's one called The Next Mozart."},{"start":191.68,"end":196.18,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"It's like a piano playing game. My niece is always playing it."},{"start":196.18,"end":202.6,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Yeah, that is a good topic. I'll definitely accept it for the next edition. These computer"},{"start":202.6,"end":207.96,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"games for learning are really popular. Right, and what have you got for us, Iris?"},{"start":208.54,"end":212.62,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Well, I've been looking at games that young children play in the playground."},{"start":213.1,"end":217.18,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Do you mean like playground games? Yeah, that's right. Playground games."},{"start":217.94,"end":224.5,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"I was thinking of looking at some examples, you know, like Catch the Dragon and, um,"},{"start":224.5,"end":232.32,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Fingers Out. Oh, yeah. Did you say Fingers Out? I remember Fingers Out. I used to play that"},{"start":232.32,"end":237.82,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"all the time when I was at primary school. What was the first game called again? Um,"},{"start":238.1,"end":243.42,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"The Dragon One. Catch the Dragon. Oh, right. Not sure if I ever played that one."},{"start":243.62,"end":247.74,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Oh, I did. Definitely. Anyway, this is a great topic, Iris."},{"start":248.18,"end":253.5,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"So you accept it? Yep, definitely. Playground games are fun to watch."},{"start":253.5,"end":260.34,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Lots and lots of fun to watch. So right back to you, Dan. Uh, any other contributions?"},{"start":261.04,"end":265.72,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Yes. So something I've been looking at is computer games for animals."},{"start":266.6,"end":271.8,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"I think it would be nice to contrast human games with like games animals play."},{"start":272.64,"end":277.66,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Well, it sounds interesting. What do you mean by computer games for animals exactly?"},{"start":277.66,"end":284.92,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Well, there's loads of videos on the internet. Darks and cats jumping at moving objects on the"},{"start":284.92,"end":291.36,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"computer screen. It's really funny. There's this one game you can get for computer tablets called"},{"start":291.36,"end":297.12,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Crazy Cat. It's brilliant. The cat chases a red dot around the screen."},{"start":298.34,"end":301.96,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Dan, you're not getting paid to look at funny videos on the internet."},{"start":301.96,"end":309.66,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"What research have you done? Really? Crazy Cat? Um, no research. Sorry."},{"start":310.67,"end":314.67,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Will you accept my topic though? Dan, you haven't done any research,"},{"start":315.01,"end":318.95,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"so it's a no. I can't accept topics that haven't been researched."},{"start":319.67,"end":326.21,"speaker":"Editorial meeting","text":"Yeah, okay. That is the end of task one."},{"start":327.58,"end":330.88,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."}],"2":[{"start":0.04,"end":7.39,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task two. Iris is working on an online game for the next issue of the magazine."},{"start":8.55,"end":16.47,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"There are three parts to task two. In part A, Iris explains the game to Dan."},{"start":17.56,"end":26.86,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"In part B, Dan plays the game. In part C, Dan and Iris discuss the game."},{"start":28.16,"end":33.6,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task. At the end of the task,"},{"start":34.16,"end":71.28,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"you will have one minute to tidy up your answers. Part A. Fill in the missing information"},{"start":71.28,"end":75.56,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"in the spaces provided in the monster maze key."},{"start":82.43,"end":87.23,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Hey Iris, what are you working on? Well, for this edition of the magazine,"},{"start":87.73,"end":93.05,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"I'm designing some games. You know, so that our subscribers can play them on their phone."},{"start":93.63,"end":98.73,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"The idea is that they pay money to play and they can win money if they win."},{"start":99.43,"end":105.73,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Cool. What kind of games? Well, the one I'm working on just now is called monster maze."},{"start":106.31,"end":111.95,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Have a look. That's the key. I'm just finishing the example for the key just now."},{"start":112.68,"end":115,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Hmm. The grid looks good."},{"start":115.34,"end":120.92,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay, good. So where's the entrance to the maze? Is it at the top here?"},{"start":120.92,"end":128.28,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"No, the other way round. The entrance to the maze is at the bottom where the numbers 1 to 6 are."},{"start":129.02,"end":134.38,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Ah, I see. Where the numbers are. So the exit to the maze is at the top then?"},{"start":134.68,"end":137.02,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Exactly. The exit's at the top."},{"start":137.28,"end":143.4,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Oh, okay. Right. And the grey squares must be walls or something."},{"start":143.84,"end":147.38,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yes, that's right. The grey squares are the walls of the maze."},{"start":147.38,"end":153.2,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"And those circles, the O's, that indicates the route you've taken through the maze."},{"start":153.92,"end":158.99,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Oh, I see the O's. And what's this M here?"},{"start":159.53,"end":164.45,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"That's the monster. There are three, but they're hidden when you play the game."},{"start":164.91,"end":169.67,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"But when you land on one of the monsters, an M appears and you lose a life."},{"start":169.97,"end":172.97,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Right. Still not sure if I get it."},{"start":173.31,"end":175.85,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"So have a look at the example in the key."},{"start":175.85,"end":184.73,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. Well, in the example, the player starts on A4, goes forward one square to B4,"},{"start":185.55,"end":195.19,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"moves left one square to B3, moves forward three squares to E3, and then moves left one square."},{"start":195.97,"end":199.43,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"And there at E2, he lands on the monster."},{"start":199.91,"end":201.13,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"N is dead."},{"start":201.27,"end":201.67,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yep."},{"start":202.39,"end":203.35,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Eden alive."},{"start":203.75,"end":204.33,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Exactly."},{"start":211.61,"end":220.75,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Part B. Plot Dan's route by putting a circle in each square like the example shown above"},{"start":220.75,"end":227.43,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"in the monster maze key, and put an M if he lands on a hidden monster."},{"start":234.18,"end":235.78,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"So, do you want to play, Dan?"},{"start":236.14,"end":236.52,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Sure."},{"start":237.02,"end":243.22,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. We can do it without the computer just now. So, I'll hide three monsters on the grid"},{"start":243.22,"end":248.26,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"by writing down the grid number, and you have to go from the entrance of the maze"},{"start":248.26,"end":253.54,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"and reach the exit without walking into the monsters. You get two lives."},{"start":254.16,"end":256.8,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Sure. So, this is my first life, eh?"},{"start":257.12,"end":259.91,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yeah. Come on. Go."},{"start":260.21,"end":265.03,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay, okay. I'm thinking. I'll start on A4."},{"start":265.73,"end":269.13,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. You're fine. Next move."},{"start":269.61,"end":274.85,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"I'll move forward one square, then move right two squares."},{"start":275.17,"end":277.69,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Gotcha. You've landed on my monster."},{"start":279.16,"end":282.3,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. So..."},{"start":282.74,"end":284.2,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Your second life."},{"start":284.54,"end":291.9,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Right. My second life. Here goes. I'll start at A5. I move forward one square."},{"start":292.68,"end":296.5,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Now, um, I'll move left two squares."},{"start":296.98,"end":298.84,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. You're fine."},{"start":299.32,"end":305.24,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Move forward three squares. And, and, move right one square."},{"start":305.96,"end":311.02,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. Here goes. Move forward one square. Did I make it?"},{"start":311.3,"end":315.38,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yes. Well done, Dan. You made it. You survived the maze."},{"start":315.84,"end":319.9,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Hooray! I won. No longer will I be caught a loser."},{"start":320.62,"end":323.1,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Well, I don't know about that."},{"start":330.2,"end":337.31,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Part C. Listen to Iris and Dan's discussion and answer the questions."},{"start":338.8,"end":342.76,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Please note, you do not have to answer in full sentences."},{"start":349.76,"end":351.96,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"So, what do you think? Any suggestions?"},{"start":352.74,"end":359.3,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Hmm. Well, the grid's a bit boring to look at. You need to make the game look more colorful."},{"start":360,"end":365.8,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yes. It does look a bit boring. You're right. I'll ask Gabby in graphics to make it more"},{"start":365.8,"end":371.04,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"colorful. And I'd suggest having more monsters. That'll make it more challenging."},{"start":371.62,"end":375.6,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yes. I suppose adding more monsters would make it more fun too."},{"start":376.24,"end":382.3,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"But I have a question. I was just wondering how will people actually play it online? The game,"},{"start":382.54,"end":388.44,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"I mean. Well, we're going to allow two ways of playing the game. The first one is by"},{"start":388.44,"end":395.24,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"actually speaking like we did. Oh, that's quite cool. So, you speak to your smartphone"},{"start":395.24,"end":400.1,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"and it marks your root on the grid? Yes, that's right. All voice controlled."},{"start":400.84,"end":403.78,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"The second way is that you can simply touch the screen."},{"start":404.18,"end":410.34,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Yes. I can imagine this working well with like touch screen devices like smartphones."},{"start":411.1,"end":415.22,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"But how can people be sure that the game's not cheating and, you know,"},{"start":415.44,"end":418.72,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"just placing the monsters after the player makes a move?"},{"start":419.3,"end":425.34,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"This is the tricky part. It's done in steps. So, in the first step, when the game starts,"},{"start":425.86,"end":428.36,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"the game sends a document to the player's phone."},{"start":428.66,"end":431.14,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. So, what happens after that?"},{"start":431.9,"end":437.18,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Right. The second step is that when the game's over, a password appears on the screen."},{"start":437.72,"end":441.68,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. Right. And then, what's the password for?"},{"start":442.08,"end":447.24,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Right. So, the third step is that the player opens the document with the password."},{"start":447.24,"end":452.44,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. Cool. So, they open the document in the third step."},{"start":453.12,"end":458.08,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Then the fourth and final step is that the player checks the location of the monsters."},{"start":458.44,"end":463.2,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Okay. That is clever. So, when the player checks the location,"},{"start":463.54,"end":466.44,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"he knows then that the game hasn't been cheating."},{"start":466.9,"end":467.46,"speaker":"Iris and Dan","text":"Exactly."},{"start":470.18,"end":476.52,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of task two. You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."}],"3":[{"start":0,"end":8.89,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Three. Katie is at the airport. She is calling Dan to ask him to edit an article she has been working"},{"start":8.89,"end":19.12,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"on. There are three parts to task three. In part A, you have to correct some sentences."},{"start":21.09,"end":25.77,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"In part B, you have to provide labels for parts of a painting."},{"start":26.8,"end":30.54,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"And in part C, you have to complete a text."},{"start":32.01,"end":38.71,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study task three. At the end of the task,"},{"start":39.07,"end":78.49,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"you will have one minute to tidy up your answers. Part A. Each line of the text below"},{"start":78.49,"end":87.08,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"may have one mistake. Correct the mistake as shown below. If the line is correct,"},{"start":87.84,"end":94.01,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"then put a tick in the right-hand column. The first has been provided as an example."},{"start":100.85,"end":101.37,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Hello."},{"start":101.99,"end":102.97,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, hi, Dan."},{"start":103.27,"end":104.59,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Hi. Where are you?"},{"start":104.89,"end":109.79,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I'm at the airport. Look, Dan, I've written this article about games and art,"},{"start":110.13,"end":116.41,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"but didn't have time to finish editing it. And like an idiot, I forgot my laptop."},{"start":117.15,"end":122.55,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I need you to check some things for me. Can you open up the file? It's in the Dropbox folder."},{"start":123.23,"end":127.57,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Sure. Okay. Let me just open it up. Right. I'm ready."},{"start":127.57,"end":132.79,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Okay. At the start of the article, I discuss a famous painting called"},{"start":132.79,"end":136.67,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Children's Games by Peter Bruegel, the Elder."},{"start":137.59,"end":140.23,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"It says here that it is a drawing."},{"start":140.81,"end":143.55,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"That should be a painting. Can you change it?"},{"start":143.97,"end":146.57,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Okay. Done."},{"start":147.39,"end":150.89,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Okay. Now, can you double check some of the facts are written correctly?"},{"start":151.51,"end":159.97,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I might have got the dates wrong, so please change it to 1560 if that's printed incorrectly."},{"start":161.09,"end":166.05,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"No, no, it's right. You say here that it was started in 1560."},{"start":167.15,"end":171.49,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Ah, just as well you said that. It was completed then."},{"start":172.13,"end":175.63,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, and check that I've spelled the artist's first name right."},{"start":175.63,"end":185.21,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"It should be Peter Bruegel and Peter spelled P-I-E-T-E-R."},{"start":185.71,"end":191.49,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, you've actually written Pete Bruegel. P-E-T-E."},{"start":191.63,"end":192.73,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Thought so."},{"start":193.17,"end":196.37,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Okay. Let me just change that now. Okay."},{"start":196.97,"end":202.79,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Right. And make sure I've got the countries right. I can never remember where he was born and died."},{"start":203.51,"end":207.65,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"He died in Belgium and was born in the Netherlands. Got it?"},{"start":208.15,"end":209.43,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yeah, I think so."},{"start":225.81,"end":237.28,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Okay. Now, the next thing is that I've put some labels on the painting"},{"start":237.28,"end":241.88,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"to point out interesting details about what the children are actually doing."},{"start":241.88,"end":246.4,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Um, the games they're playing, I mean. I didn't manage to finish them."},{"start":246.92,"end":248.84,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Could you add them as I go through them?"},{"start":249.48,"end":253.26,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yes, let's see. I've got the picture up here now."},{"start":254.66,"end":259.2,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"So, if you look closely, there's one boy sitting cross-legged on the grass."},{"start":260.06,"end":265.1,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Well, this was actually a form of exercise at the time, a bit like yoga today."},{"start":265.74,"end":271.14,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Okay. I can see that now. It does look like he's doing a yoga exercise."},{"start":271.14,"end":273.36,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I didn't realise before."},{"start":274.28,"end":278.08,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Also, in the picture, there are girls holding a basket."},{"start":278.68,"end":283.38,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh yes, I see them. Seems to be a basket of fruit or something."},{"start":284.22,"end":287.82,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"So, what are they doing then? It doesn't look like a game."},{"start":288.28,"end":291.42,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Well, they're actually performing a wedding, a pretend wedding."},{"start":291.88,"end":297.32,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, I remember having to dress up for pretend weddings when I was little with my big sister."},{"start":297.88,"end":301.56,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, now that would be a wedding picture I'd love to see."},{"start":301.8,"end":302.78,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yeah, well."},{"start":303.18,"end":307.72,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Now, what else? Okay, you see those boys on top of the fence?"},{"start":308.66,"end":310.68,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Well, they're playing at riding horses."},{"start":311.58,"end":317.1,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh yes, I can see that now. They really do look like they are riding a horse."},{"start":317.84,"end":320.98,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"So, what about the kids jumping over the other kids' legs?"},{"start":321.7,"end":322.52,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"What's that about?"},{"start":322.96,"end":324.96,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"This game's actually quite painful."},{"start":324.96,"end":329.94,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"The children would apparently kick very hard and it would really hurt."},{"start":330.46,"end":332.7,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Ouch! So, it's a kicking game."},{"start":333.46,"end":335.94,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I'm glad we didn't play that when I was at school."},{"start":336.82,"end":338.48,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"We did something similar, actually."},{"start":339.12,"end":341.74,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Kicking people, I mean. It was quite violent."},{"start":342.48,"end":342.8,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Really?"},{"start":350.07,"end":353.41,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Part C. Complete the text."},{"start":354.44,"end":357.66,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Write one or more words in each gap."},{"start":364.48,"end":367.24,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Right, moving on. What else is there?"},{"start":367.24,"end":373.3,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, oh yes. At the end of the article, there's a section on present-day games."},{"start":373.94,"end":376.6,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Games that use classic art for their graphics."},{"start":377.08,"end":378.5,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I didn't quite finish that."},{"start":378.86,"end":380.94,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Oh, okay. They look fun."},{"start":381.48,"end":383.3,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yeah, I loved reading up on this."},{"start":383.74,"end":388.24,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"I like the fact that they're making a video game out of a classic work of art"},{"start":388.24,"end":391.04,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"like The Last Supper or The Mona Lisa."},{"start":391.9,"end":394.02,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yeah, I know. They're brilliant, aren't they?"},{"start":394.02,"end":399.5,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"So, what's interesting is that these games use 8-bit graphics."},{"start":400,"end":403.76,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"8-bit? You mean like early computer graphics?"},{"start":404.62,"end":408.12,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Why use 8-bit graphics? That's a bit weird."},{"start":408.66,"end":411.42,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Well, because for the game designers, it's a challenge."},{"start":412.04,"end":418.28,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"They're trying to use these little blocks with only a few colours to create very complex pictures."},{"start":418.28,"end":419.18,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Hmm."},{"start":420.12,"end":423.64,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"What I mean is that they, the designers of these computer games,"},{"start":424.1,"end":431.08,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"enjoy making these really complicated images from small blocks using only a small number of colours."},{"start":431.88,"end":436.32,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yeah, okay. Well, let me just finish making a note of that."},{"start":437.26,"end":438.66,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Right, keep going."},{"start":439.38,"end":444.04,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"So, the games themselves are actually quite simple, like really, really simple,"},{"start":444.22,"end":445.62,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"and there's a reason for that."},{"start":446.16,"end":447.2,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"And what's the reason?"},{"start":447.2,"end":452.26,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Well, these games are not meant to be serious. They're just supposed to be funny."},{"start":452.96,"end":456.2,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"You mean humorous funny, not weird funny?"},{"start":456.5,"end":458.48,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yeah, exactly, like a joke."},{"start":459.02,"end":462.74,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"And where can you find these games? Do you have to pay for them?"},{"start":463.14,"end":466.54,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"You can get them on the internet. The good thing is they're free."},{"start":467.06,"end":468.16,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"You don't need to pay anything."},{"start":468.74,"end":471.12,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Free? Well, that makes a change."},{"start":471.78,"end":474.37,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Maybe I'll check them out. Is that everything?"},{"start":474.37,"end":477.49,"speaker":"Kaity and Dan","text":"Yes, that's all. Thanks for helping out, Dan."}],"4":[{"start":35.02,"end":38.96,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task."},{"start":40.28,"end":44.8,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"At the end of the task, you will have three minutes to tidy up your answers."},{"start":77.68,"end":84.16,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Hi. Well, today I'm joined by Dr Jonathan Newman from the University of Jeong Yi An."},{"start":84.52,"end":85.24,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Good morning."},{"start":85.74,"end":90.54,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"And Dr Natalie Sum from the University of Eastern Australia."},{"start":91.04,"end":91.86,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Good morning, Katie."},{"start":92.78,"end":97.26,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Our discussion today is about the psychology of games and play."},{"start":98,"end":99.7,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"So let's dive in, shall we?"},{"start":100.46,"end":104.06,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Can we define what a game is, first of all? Jonathan?"},{"start":105.2,"end":106.88,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Help. That's a challenge."},{"start":107.6,"end":112.94,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Well, we may say that most games have at least two key aspects in common."},{"start":113.46,"end":116.22,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"First, they provide some form of entertainment."},{"start":116.94,"end":120.16,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"We seek out games primarily for pleasure and fun."},{"start":120.96,"end":125.4,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"The second thing is that they seem to have some outcome or goal."},{"start":126.04,"end":130.28,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"For instance, you either win or lose a game or finish it in some way."},{"start":131.04,"end":132.16,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Would you agree with that, Natalie?"},{"start":132.74,"end":133.38,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Yes, Jonathan."},{"start":134.16,"end":138.08,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Well, it's certainly true that games are primarily for entertainment"},{"start":138.66,"end":141.16,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"and that games all have some kind of outcome."},{"start":141.86,"end":143.86,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"I would like to add a third aspect."},{"start":144.78,"end":148.9,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Would you agree with me that games must follow some set of rules, too?"},{"start":149.74,"end":155.14,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Yes, I'd agree that following rules would be an essential element of games in general."},{"start":155.4,"end":161.34,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"You know, Jonathan, to me, what's most fascinating is how games and life are so similar."},{"start":162.1,"end":165.08,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"I'd even say life itself is but a game."},{"start":166,"end":166.8,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Life is a game?"},{"start":167.22,"end":169.2,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"I hope you don't actually mean that."},{"start":169.74,"end":170.66,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"But it is, is it not?"},{"start":171.54,"end":174.04,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Life is simply a game we all have to play."},{"start":174.74,"end":176.22,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Maybe your life's a game, Natalie."},{"start":176.92,"end":177.46,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Mine isn't."},{"start":177.8,"end":180.14,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"And I don't think anyone else's is either."},{"start":180.7,"end":182.06,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Actually, not even yours."},{"start":182.62,"end":186.9,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Jonathan, your problem is you need to get some more fun in life."},{"start":187.36,"end":187.74,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"I mean..."},{"start":187.74,"end":190.6,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Okay, let's leave that point there."},{"start":191.32,"end":196.8,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Now, both of you have done a great deal of research into games and play in animals."},{"start":197.36,"end":198.74,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Would you like to give some examples?"},{"start":199.52,"end":199.7,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Sure."},{"start":200.38,"end":202.66,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Well, here's something that'll surprise you."},{"start":203.2,"end":205.46,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Do you know ants play fight?"},{"start":205.88,"end":206.96,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"No, really?"},{"start":207.58,"end":208.08,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Ants?"},{"start":208.48,"end":209,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Oh, yes."},{"start":209.4,"end":210.04,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"That's right."},{"start":210.52,"end":211.86,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"It helps them fight better."},{"start":212.16,"end":213.24,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"It's really true."},{"start":214.32,"end":214.96,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"That's incredible."},{"start":215.24,"end":219.68,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"So they actually get better at real fighting from play fighting."},{"start":220.28,"end":221.72,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Here's another one that gets me."},{"start":222.56,"end":223.08,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Fish play."},{"start":223.68,"end":226.48,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"You know, sometimes when you're watching fish in a pond"},{"start":226.48,"end":229.26,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"and they suddenly jump out for no apparent reason."},{"start":229.76,"end":230.84,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Yeah, I've seen that."},{"start":231.24,"end":232.92,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"I thought they'd jump to catch food."},{"start":233.1,"end":235.46,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"No, no, they jump for the fun of it."},{"start":236.18,"end":237.98,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Most fish feed underwater."},{"start":238.62,"end":241.68,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"But this play jumping helps them in certain situations"},{"start":241.68,"end":245.04,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"like if they have to escape something trying to eat them."},{"start":245.78,"end":250.2,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Yes, apparently jumping helps them escape from predators and hunters."},{"start":250.98,"end":254.86,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"But to me, what's really fascinating is how playing games"},{"start":254.86,"end":258.34,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"actually develop morality in all kinds of animals."},{"start":258.9,"end":259.84,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Can you give an example?"},{"start":260.58,"end":264.06,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Well, rats often engage in play fighting games."},{"start":264.58,"end":266.28,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"There are three points to note here."},{"start":266.78,"end":271.52,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"First, play fighting games occur between stronger and weaker rats."},{"start":271.68,"end":274.82,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"So one rat will always be stronger than another rat."},{"start":275.32,"end":275.66,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Precisely."},{"start":276.14,"end":278.96,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"I mean, the same is true in any kind of game."},{"start":279.56,"end":283.88,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Someone will always be a bit better or a bit worse than the other player."},{"start":284.52,"end":286.88,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Now, the second point is where it gets interesting."},{"start":287.58,"end":291.28,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"If the weaker rat always loses, it will stop playing."},{"start":292.08,"end":293.56,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"You mean the weaker rat says,"},{"start":294.04,"end":297.62,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"right, I'm not playing this game if you keep winning."},{"start":298.46,"end":301.92,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"That's how I feel when I play scrabble or chess with my daughter."},{"start":303.08,"end":305.1,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Now, for the third and most interesting part,"},{"start":305.68,"end":309.4,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"the stronger rat learns that it has to let the weaker rat win"},{"start":309.4,"end":312,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"some of the time so they can keep playing."},{"start":312.6,"end":317.16,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Oh, so the stronger rat will deliberately lose to the weaker rat."},{"start":317.84,"end":320.1,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Otherwise, it'll have no friends to play with."},{"start":320.46,"end":323.5,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Oh, poor strong rat with no friends."},{"start":324.16,"end":327.1,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"So I guess they are learning something very important from this."},{"start":327.1,"end":327.86,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Absolutely."},{"start":328.84,"end":331.76,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"For one thing, they are developing a kind of morality."},{"start":332.82,"end":336.24,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"The second thing is that they learn how to live together peacefully."},{"start":336.88,"end":338.36,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Wow, that's amazing."},{"start":339.08,"end":340.96,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"So rats have to learn to be moral"},{"start":340.96,"end":344.36,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"and they have to learn how to live peacefully with one another,"},{"start":344.9,"end":346.76,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"just like us humans have to do."},{"start":347.32,"end":349.18,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"That's absolutely fascinating."},{"start":350.26,"end":352.68,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Okay, well, we're going to have a short break."},{"start":353.2,"end":354.28,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"And when we come back,"},{"start":354.28,"end":357.64,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"Natalie and Jonathan will be answering some of your questions."},{"start":360.3,"end":365.64,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of task four and of part 3a."},{"start":366.73,"end":371.67,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have three minutes to complete your answers to task four"},{"start":372.23,"end":375.19,"speaker":"Podcast guests","text":"and to tidy up all your other answers."}]},"partB":[{"start":0.03,"end":3.29,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Look at page two of your data file."},{"start":7.4,"end":8.7,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"You are Sami Tsung."},{"start":9.37,"end":11.94,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"You work for a board game company called"},{"start":11.94,"end":14.02,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Griffin Workshop in Hong Kong."},{"start":15.03,"end":17.97,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"It is a small company set up by some friends."},{"start":19.34,"end":21.98,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"It is now working on its latest board game,"},{"start":22.56,"end":24.28,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Escape to Hong Kong Island."},{"start":25.65,"end":30.27,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Your boss, Angel Fu, has asked you to do some tasks."},{"start":32.84,"end":37.44,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"You will listen to a recording of the weekly podcast program, The Classical."},{"start":38.81,"end":44.17,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"In the podcast, you will hear an interview with Angel Fu and Eric Park,"},{"start":44.73,"end":46.75,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"a well-known board game designer."},{"start":48.21,"end":50.91,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Take notes under the appropriate headings."},{"start":54.07,"end":57.89,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Before the recording is played, you will have five minutes"},{"start":57.89,"end":61.69,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"to study the question answer book and the data file"},{"start":61.69,"end":66.19,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"to familiarize yourself with the situation and the tasks."},{"start":66.19,"end":71.51,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Complete the tasks by following the instructions"},{"start":71.51,"end":75.37,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"in the question answer book and on the recording."},{"start":76.46,"end":81.18,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"You will find all the information you need in the question answer book,"},{"start":81.94,"end":84.52,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"the data file, and on the recording."},{"start":86.92,"end":92.44,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"As you listen, you can make notes on page three of the data file."},{"start":94.18,"end":97.66,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have five minutes to familiarize yourself"},{"start":97.66,"end":101.44,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"with the question answer book and the data file."},{"start":403.75,"end":405.73,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"The recording is about to begin."},{"start":406.92,"end":410.02,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Turn to page three of the data file."},{"start":446.78,"end":450.26,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Hi, David. Glad to be in Hong Kong."},{"start":451.43,"end":456.79,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So, Angel, I understand that you've started your own local board game company."},{"start":457.07,"end":457.63,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"That's right."},{"start":458.19,"end":459.67,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"And what's the name of your company?"},{"start":460.27,"end":461.05,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Griffin Workshop."},{"start":462.13,"end":464.25,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So, why did you decide to start your company?"},{"start":464.91,"end":467.11,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, we're four friends at the same time."},{"start":467.11,"end":472.79,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"I mean, all four of us, we really wanted to make our own board games."},{"start":473.29,"end":477.95,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So, that was why you started then, because you wanted to make your own board games?"},{"start":478.29,"end":481.71,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes. And we thought, why not start a games company?"},{"start":482.45,"end":484.13,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"And so, there are four of you."},{"start":484.43,"end":486.59,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"That's right. Oh, wait a minute."},{"start":487.43,"end":489.89,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"There's actually five members of the company."},{"start":490.49,"end":493.77,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"We recently employed a new person, Sami Dung."},{"start":494.31,"end":496.09,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"If you're listening, hi, Sami."},{"start":496.71,"end":498.21,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So, you're all from Hong Kong?"},{"start":498.65,"end":499.41,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes, that's right."},{"start":499.93,"end":500.99,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Hong Kong born and bred."},{"start":501.65,"end":503.57,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, it's nice to see a local company."},{"start":504.43,"end":505.51,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"When did you form the company?"},{"start":506.01,"end":508.27,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Two years ago, in 2016."},{"start":508.95,"end":511.21,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. So, quite a new company."},{"start":512.3,"end":515.04,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So, Eric, Angel's company just started out."},{"start":515.56,"end":517,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"They have an idea for a game."},{"start":517.62,"end":518.74,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"They want to move ahead."},{"start":519.71,"end":521.97,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"What advice would you give her and her company?"},{"start":522.8,"end":525.78,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, supposing that you have developed a game."},{"start":525.78,"end":527.36,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes, yes, we have."},{"start":528.32,"end":530.68,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Right. Well, the next stage is, obviously,"},{"start":531.24,"end":534.36,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"that you need to decide how to get funds to make your game."},{"start":535.14,"end":537.04,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Ah, of course. Money."},{"start":537.96,"end":541.88,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes. Well, a small company needs to get funds to produce the game,"},{"start":542.06,"end":545,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"because producing the game can be quite expensive."},{"start":545.6,"end":549.52,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"And I personally think that the best way to get funds is through Game Start."},{"start":550.18,"end":553.04,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Oh, okay. And what is Game Start?"},{"start":553.04,"end":558.72,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, Game Start is the most well-known funding website for board game companies."},{"start":559.7,"end":564.44,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Right. So, what's the main advantage of using Game Start as a source of funds, then?"},{"start":565.2,"end":570.96,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, I'd say the main advantage of something like Game Start is it's global, so..."},{"start":570.96,"end":571.54,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Because it's online."},{"start":571.86,"end":577.6,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Exactly. So, you can get money from investors from, well, basically anywhere in the world."},{"start":578.2,"end":580.5,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. Well, that sounds the way to go."},{"start":580.5,"end":585.62,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yeah. But don't forget, there are other ways besides Game Start to get funding."},{"start":586.02,"end":586.54,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Such as?"},{"start":586.96,"end":589.34,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Like getting a grant from a local company."},{"start":589.64,"end":596.26,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. I mean, there are local grants available where you can win money as an award."},{"start":597,"end":602.5,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"In Hong Kong, one of the best-known of these is the Acorn grant. You might have heard of it?"},{"start":602.84,"end":606.56,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yeah. Actually, we've been looking into applying for the Acorn grant."},{"start":606.56,"end":612.5,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Good. Though, with a grant like the Acorn grant, there are definitely disadvantages."},{"start":613.2,"end":613.56,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Like what?"},{"start":614.24,"end":620.68,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, often when you get a grant, they tell you that they'll give you lots of help, but really,"},{"start":621.18,"end":626.38,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"they just want to control everything. The Acorn grant has the reputation for being one of those."},{"start":626.68,"end":626.94,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Really?"},{"start":627.38,"end":628.66,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yeah, I'm afraid so."},{"start":629.16,"end":634.14,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Oh, I don't want that. Me and my friends at Griffin Workshop just want to be independent."},{"start":634.14,"end":637.32,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"We don't really want other people to control us."},{"start":637.92,"end":644.54,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, if you value your independence, then a grant like the Acorn grant maybe isn't your best option."},{"start":646.16,"end":653,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. Now, Angel, back to the games that Griffin Workshop make. Have you actually made any games yet?"},{"start":653.38,"end":656.98,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yeah. We've made two games. We've published the first one,"},{"start":657.2,"end":659.42,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"and we are now working on the second one."},{"start":660.08,"end":661.58,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So tell us about the first one."},{"start":661.58,"end":665.16,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. Our first game was called Death Kick."},{"start":665.92,"end":669.58,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Death Kick. Now, that is a good name."},{"start":669.98,"end":671.68,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"And it's a card game."},{"start":672.14,"end":676.73,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"A card game. And from the sound of it, it's a fighting game, I'm guessing."},{"start":677.09,"end":679.23,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yeah. It's a Kung Fu card game."},{"start":679.39,"end":681.85,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"A Kung Fu card game. Brilliant."},{"start":682.47,"end":685.87,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yeah. I've played Death Kick, and I thought it was really good."},{"start":686.13,"end":686.81,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Oh, wow."},{"start":688.13,"end":691.53,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. Well, tell us about your second game, the latest one."},{"start":691.89,"end":698.59,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. Our latest game is called Escape to Hong Kong Island, and it's a zombie game."},{"start":699.41,"end":703.17,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"A zombie game. Okay. Is it set in Hong Kong?"},{"start":703.47,"end":705.63,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes, that's right. Set in Hong Kong."},{"start":705.77,"end":707.91,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. So what happens in the game?"},{"start":708.51,"end":711.97,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Right. Well, the players start in Kowloon, and…"},{"start":711.97,"end":713.43,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. They're in Kowloon."},{"start":713.43,"end":716.65,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes. And the players have to reach Hong Kong Island."},{"start":717.31,"end":720.09,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"And so the first player who gets to Hong Kong Island is the winner?"},{"start":720.61,"end":726.71,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Actually, no. It's a team game, so everybody in your team has to reach Hong Kong Island."},{"start":727.51,"end":732.39,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"So if everybody in your team reaches Hong Kong Island, your team is the winner? Is that the idea?"},{"start":732.61,"end":737.97,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"That's right. If all your team members manage to get to Hong Kong Island, that's it. You've won."},{"start":738.61,"end":743.08,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Sounds good. So, Eric, as an experienced game designer,"},{"start":743.46,"end":746.7,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"what advice would you give Angel about Escape to Hong Kong Island?"},{"start":747.52,"end":753.16,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, it sounds pretty interesting. I would say that the first thing you need to do is be very"},{"start":753.16,"end":759.22,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"clear who your target audience is. Who's your target audience for the game, Angel?"},{"start":759.96,"end":760.6,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Young teenagers."},{"start":761.16,"end":767.86,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. Well, a word of warning then. Young teenagers is often the trickiest age group"},{"start":767.86,"end":772.84,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"to sell a game to. And has your artist designed some of the artwork yet?"},{"start":772.84,"end":775.26,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Yes. We have samples of artwork."},{"start":776.99,"end":782.71,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, okay. One thing to always remember if your audience is young teenagers is that parents"},{"start":782.71,"end":786.63,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"usually have the final say in whether the game gets bought or not."},{"start":787.11,"end":787.73,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Oh, okay."},{"start":788.29,"end":793.29,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"I mean, either parents themselves buy it for their kids for something like a birthday present,"},{"start":793.55,"end":797.95,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"or they'll demand to see what their son or daughter has bought."},{"start":798.45,"end":798.93,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Oh."},{"start":799.6,"end":803.26,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Very often, you have to remind your artist about this."},{"start":803.48,"end":809.54,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Sometimes an artist will often get carried away, and they'll produce this beautiful work, and"},{"start":809.54,"end":813.88,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"that may well appeal to the young teenager, but the parents won't"},{"start":813.88,"end":816.22,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"approve because it's just too graphic."},{"start":817.04,"end":818.3,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"And by graphic, you mean?"},{"start":818.84,"end":822.78,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Too adult. Art that's just too violent, usually."},{"start":823.58,"end":826.66,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Parents won't buy, or won't let their kids buy it."},{"start":827.24,"end":829.92,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Well, that's some pretty sound advice for you there, Angel."},{"start":830.7,"end":836.38,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Okay. I think we're out of time now, and I'd like to thank you both for coming in to chat to us today."},{"start":838.84,"end":842.24,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of the listening component of this paper."},{"start":843.37,"end":849.17,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"You will now have one hour and fifteen minutes to complete the written tasks"},{"start":849.17,"end":857.9,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"in either Part B1 or Part B2. An announcement will be made when time is up."},{"start":859.3,"end":862.78,"speaker":"The Classical guests","text":"Take off your earphones now and turn off the radio."}]});})();
